1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,609
A theme decides how the pages of an Orchard Core site look.

2
00:00:04,609 --> 00:00:08,939
In this video, you generate a theme project from a template, describe it

3
00:00:08,939 --> 00:00:11,660
in its manifest, and apply it to your site.

4
00:00:16,260 --> 00:00:19,898
A theme is a project in your solution that holds the layout, the

5
00:00:19,898 --> 00:00:24,471
templates, and the static files, such as stylesheets and images, that Orchard Core

6
00:00:24,471 --> 00:00:26,030
uses to render the site.

7
00:00:26,780 --> 00:00:28,464
A site uses two themes:

8
00:00:28,464 --> 00:00:32,937
a site theme for the front end, and an admin theme for the admin pages.

9
00:00:32,937 --> 00:00:38,803
The Themes module, under Design, Themes, lists the themes of your application and applies them.

10
00:00:38,803 --> 00:00:41,010
This video creates a site theme.

11
00:00:41,760 --> 00:00:44,785
The template creates a theme with three parts:

12
00:00:44,785 --> 00:00:48,916
a project file that marks the project as a theme, a manifest that

13
00:00:48,916 --> 00:00:52,116
describes it, and a layout that wraps every page.

14
00:00:52,116 --> 00:00:53,570
Let's generate one.

15
00:00:57,770 --> 00:01:02,261
The project template for themes is part of the Orchard Core project templates

16
00:01:02,261 --> 00:01:06,211
package, which also has templates for web applications and modules.

17
00:01:06,211 --> 00:01:09,890
Install the package once, with the dotnet new install command.

18
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:15,577
In the folder of your solution, next to the web application, run dotnet

19
00:01:15,577 --> 00:01:18,399
new octheme with a name for the theme.

20
00:01:18,399 --> 00:01:21,220
Here, the name is MyTheme.OrchardCore.

21
00:01:21,970 --> 00:01:27,383
The name becomes the folder, the project file, and the identifier of the theme.

22
00:01:27,383 --> 00:01:29,867
The template creates three files:

23
00:01:29,867 --> 00:01:35,790
the project file, Manifest.cs, and a Liquid layout, Layout.liquid, in the Views folder.

24
00:01:36,540 --> 00:01:40,716
AddLiquid is one of the template options, and it is true by default.

25
00:01:40,716 --> 00:01:44,610
Set to false, it leaves out the Liquid layout, for a theme that

26
00:01:44,610 --> 00:01:46,190
uses Razor views only.

27
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:50,575
Add the project to the solution, then add a reference to it from

28
00:01:50,575 --> 00:01:54,210
the web application, so that the application includes the theme.

29
00:01:58,410 --> 00:02:02,667
The project file references the Orchard Core Theme Targets package.

30
00:02:02,667 --> 00:02:06,749
It marks the project as a theme, and embeds the views and static

31
00:02:06,749 --> 00:02:09,140
files of the theme in the assembly.

32
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:14,780
The Razor SDK lets the theme use Razor templates as well as Liquid ones.

33
00:02:14,780 --> 00:02:18,793
If a theme has Razor views but does not use the Razor SDK,

34
00:02:18,793 --> 00:02:21,050
the build stops with an error.

35
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:24,519
Manifest.cs holds the Theme attribute.

36
00:02:24,519 --> 00:02:30,574
Orchard Core reads the name, author, website, version, and description of the theme from it.

37
00:02:30,574 --> 00:02:35,147
The template sets the name and description to the name you gave, and

38
00:02:35,147 --> 00:02:38,360
fills in its own author, website, and version.

39
00:02:39,110 --> 00:02:41,209
Layout.liquid is the layout.

40
00:02:41,209 --> 00:02:46,890
The render_body tag outputs the content of the page being rendered, and render_section

41
00:02:46,890 --> 00:02:49,792
outputs a named section, here the Footer.

42
00:02:49,792 --> 00:02:54,300
The page_title tag writes the page title, with the site name first.

43
00:02:55,050 --> 00:03:00,890
The resources tags output the meta tags, stylesheets, and scripts that modules register,

44
00:03:00,890 --> 00:03:02,941
so keep them in the layout.

45
00:03:02,941 --> 00:03:07,290
A comment in the template reads, insert required resources here.

46
00:03:08,040 --> 00:03:12,233
A script tag near the end of the layout requests jQuery for the

47
00:03:12,233 --> 00:03:13,630
foot of the page.

48
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:20,895
Replace the values of the template with your own.

49
00:03:20,895 --> 00:03:24,852
Here, MyTheme has an author, a website, a description, and a tag.

50
00:03:24,852 --> 00:03:28,530
The Themes page shows these values on the card of the theme.

51
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:34,358
Name is the title of the card, and the identifier stays the name of the assembly.

52
00:03:34,358 --> 00:03:36,342
Tags appear on the card too.

53
00:03:36,342 --> 00:03:39,261
On the Themes page, two tags have a meaning:

54
00:03:39,261 --> 00:03:43,580
Admin marks an admin theme, and hidden keeps the theme off the page.

55
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:48,449
To give the card a thumbnail, add a file named Theme.png to the

56
00:03:48,449 --> 00:03:50,956
wwwroot folder of the theme project.

57
00:03:50,956 --> 00:03:55,254
Orchard Core serves it from the static files of the theme, and the

58
00:03:55,254 --> 00:03:57,940
Themes page shows it as the card image.

59
00:03:58,690 --> 00:04:04,129
Files in the wwwroot folder, such as stylesheets, scripts, and images, are served

60
00:04:04,129 --> 00:04:06,629
under the identifier of the theme.

61
00:04:06,629 --> 00:04:09,630
The layout can refer to them by that path.

62
00:04:13,841 --> 00:04:17,367
Build and run the web application, and open the admin.

63
00:04:17,367 --> 00:04:22,361
In the admin menu, Design, Themes lists the themes of the application as cards.

64
00:04:22,813 --> 00:04:25,084
Here is the card of MyTheme.

65
00:04:25,084 --> 00:04:30,827
It shows the thumbnail from Theme.png, the name and description, and the author,

66
00:04:30,827 --> 00:04:34,233
website, tags, and version from the manifest.

67
00:04:34,696 --> 00:04:36,576
The card has two buttons.

68
00:04:36,576 --> 00:04:40,094
Enable turns the theme on without making it current.

69
00:04:40,094 --> 00:04:44,826
Make Current sets the theme as the site theme, and enables it if needed.

70
00:04:45,286 --> 00:04:47,006
Let's click Make Current.

71
00:04:47,006 --> 00:04:48,670
Two messages confirm it:

72
00:04:48,670 --> 00:04:52,718
MyTheme was enabled, and MyTheme was set as the default Site theme.

73
00:04:52,718 --> 00:04:56,878
The current themes come first, and the card of MyTheme reads, This is

74
00:04:56,878 --> 00:04:58,486
the current Site theme.

75
00:04:58,937 --> 00:05:00,901
Open the front end of the site.

76
00:05:00,901 --> 00:05:05,677
Its pages are rendered by the layout of MyTheme, which has no stylesheet of its own.

77
00:05:09,877 --> 00:05:15,878
To write the layout in Razor, add Layout.cshtml to Views in place of Layout.liquid.

78
00:05:15,878 --> 00:05:18,912
The project already uses the Razor SDK.

79
00:05:18,912 --> 00:05:23,767
As the built-in Razor themes do, add a view imports file to Views,

80
00:05:23,767 --> 00:05:27,947
so the layout inherits from the Orchard Core Razor page.

81
00:05:28,697 --> 00:05:33,463
To go further, separate videos cover creating a theme from an existing HTML

82
00:05:33,463 --> 00:05:38,877
template, declaring scripts and stylesheets as resources, and creating an admin theme.

83
00:05:40,877 --> 00:05:44,407
A theme is a project with a manifest and a layout, which you

84
00:05:44,407 --> 00:05:50,236
generate from the template, describe in the manifest, and apply with Make Current under Design, Themes.

85
00:05:50,236 --> 00:05:51,627
Thanks for watching.

